1
00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:04,800
Here's to us, the Moonlit Black
Cats! Cheers, everyone! Cheers!

2
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:08,540
I got another!

3
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:12,340
Here's to the guy who saved
our lives, Takirito! Takirito!

4
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:16,697
Uh, cheers, guys. Thanks.
Yeah, man. Thank you.

5
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:17,610
You saved us back there.

6
00:00:17,693 --> 00:00:18,523
Thank you.

7
00:00:18,606 --> 00:00:19,480
Thank you so much.

8
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:20,780
Uh, it's cool.

9
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:23,620
I can't tell you how scared I was,

10
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:26,817
and it made me so happy when
you came to save us, I...

11
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:29,320
Oh, well, uh, Kirito, sir?

12
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:34,805
I hope I'm not out of line asking this,
but I was wondering what level you're at.

13
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:36,540
Level 20?

14
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:38,570
Really?

15
00:00:38,653 --> 00:00:40,497
You're at our level and
still a solo player?

16
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:42,720
You're an inspiration, sir! Cait,

17
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:44,277
I'm not your superior,

18
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:47,977
and being solo means I'm always
hunting enemies out in the boonies.

19
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:49,472
It's not very efficient.

20
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:50,760
Oh, right.

21
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:52,680
Well, in that case,

22
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:54,417
I hate to spring this on you here,

23
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:57,559
but if you want, we'd love
to have you in our guild.

24
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:02,277
Our mace wielder, Tetsuo, is the only
one we can put out front right now.

25
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:04,097
And then we've got Sachi over here.

26
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:06,737
I was thinking of having her
switch to sword and shield.

27
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:09,117
That way, she can fight
on the front lines.

28
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:12,057
The thing is, she says she's
not sure she can handle it.

29
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:14,777
If you join us, maybe you
could teach her a thing or two.

30
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:15,760
Oh, come on.

31
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:17,155
I'm not that useless.

32
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:22,177
Seriously, you can't just put me up
front and expect me to know what to do.

33
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:23,260
I'd be terrified.

34
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:24,680
It's no big deal.

35
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:25,717
Just hide behind your shield.

36
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:26,630
Yeah, right.

37
00:01:26,713 --> 00:01:30,169
Ever since I can remember,
you've always been a Sigurd cat.

38
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:33,382
We always joke around like that.

39
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:34,840
See, in real life,

40
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:38,017
we all go to the same high school
and are members of the computer club.

41
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:40,437
But if you're worried about
fitting in with us, don't.

42
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:43,157
As far as I'm concerned, you're
already part of our group.

43
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:44,340
Right? Mm-hmm.

44
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:52,620
Well, I'm really flattered.

45
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:54,491
And thanks for the offer.

46
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:56,820
I'll do it.

47
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:30,920
I'm afraid of the back of my
back, but I can't believe it.

48
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:39,760
I've seen a few times in the sky.

49
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:46,100
Here it is, surely, a beautiful heart.

50
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:49,737
It's a dream.

51
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:51,580
I love you!

52
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:53,700
What do you think?

53
00:02:54,320 --> 00:03:00,577
Your body is so good I'm not
even gonna give you a chance

54
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:06,240
I'm not even looking at you
I'm not even looking at you

55
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:10,240
I'm not even looking at you

56
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:18,117
I'm not looking at you I
can't believe in my dreams,

57
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:28,480
I want to always be waiting
I'll give you everything I have

58
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:51,440
Sachi! Get back! I got this!

59
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:01,100
Come on, Tetsuo! Switch out! Got it!

60
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:08,880
All right!

61
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:10,640
Congrats, man!

62
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:12,805
You totally owned that sucker!

63
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:17,217
The assault team made
it through to floor 28.

64
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:18,917
That's amazing!

65
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:25,157
Hey Kirito, what the heck does the
assault team have that we don't? Well,

66
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:29,117
access to information—with
that they can find out the

67
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:31,777
easiest ways to get XP—and
they don't share that info.

68
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:36,417
Yeah, you're probably
right, but I think what?

69
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:39,037
think what really sets
them apart is willpower.

70
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:40,120
What do you mean?

71
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:42,677
I guess what I mean is.

72
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,657
They have the will to
stick up for their friends.

73
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:46,505
or any player for that matter.

74
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:50,117
Truth is, I like to think we
have that same kind of drive,

75
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:52,717
even though we still
need their protection.

76
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:56,257
That said, our first priority
is looking out for each other.

77
00:04:56,340 --> 00:05:01,046
But someday, if we get strong enough,
we'll join the elites in the assault team.

78
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:02,390
I see.

79
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:03,838
That's a good goal.

80
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,060
I don't know. I guess.

81
00:05:06,620 --> 00:05:08,840
Hey, leader, give me some love!

82
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:10,310
So,

83
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:12,377
you really think we can
be as strong as the Holy

84
00:05:12,460 --> 00:05:14,577
Dragon Alliance or the
Knights of the Blood Oath?

85
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:15,778
Yeah, what if I do?

86
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:20,117
Nothing wrong with setting our sights
high, but we have to be level 30 first.

87
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:21,259
That's impossible.

88
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:23,707
I like the way Cait thinks.

89
00:05:23,860 --> 00:05:27,137
If the Black Cats can level up
fast and get to the front lines,

90
00:05:27,220 --> 00:05:31,044
his ideals could change the elitist
attitude of the assault team.

91
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:38,284
I have an announcement to make.

92
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:43,800
After our latest hunts in the
field, we've got 200,000 coal.

93
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:45,150
Awesome!

94
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:48,637
Buying a house of our own doesn't
seem like such a pipe dream anymore.

95
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:49,550
I know!

96
00:05:49,633 --> 00:05:51,317
We should upgrade Sachi's equipment.

97
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:52,230
Good idea.

98
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:55,200
I'm fine with what I have.

99
00:05:55,740 --> 00:05:56,660
Oh, come on.

100
00:05:57,060 --> 00:06:00,766
You know, it's not fair to make
Kirito be out in front forever.

101
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:02,360
I'm sorry.

102
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,155
Don't worry about me.

103
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:05,560
I'm cool with it.

104
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:06,980
Thanks, Kirito.

105
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:11,857
Sachi, I know switching jobs isn't easy,
but seriously, you're almost there!

106
00:06:11,940 --> 00:06:13,620
You can do it, I know it!

107
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:34,110
Klein.

108
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:49,680
What's up, Kirito?

109
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:52,500
The trash mob's all yours, guys. Sure.

110
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:55,777
Man, it's been a while
since I've seen you.

111
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:59,036
What, you doing some late-night
leveling or something?

112
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:00,831
What's up with that icon?

113
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:02,620
Did you join a guild?

114
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,837
Yeah, I guess you could say that.

115
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:05,840
It's all clear!

116
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:07,140
We can move on!

117
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:10,430
See ya.

118
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:11,990
Yeah.

119
00:07:13,620 --> 00:07:14,900
Oh, come on.

120
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,820
Is it still bugging you?

121
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:27,070
It's Cait.

122
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:30,077
Sachi went off somewhere
and hasn't come back yet.

123
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:32,101
We're heading to the dungeon now.

124
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:34,968
Please let me know if
you find anything out.

125
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:36,910
Sachi…

126
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:58,600
Sachi?

127
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:01,630
Kirito…

128
00:08:01,713 --> 00:08:03,360
Everyone's worried about you.

129
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:11,820
Hey, Kirito. Yeah?

130
00:08:12,540 --> 00:08:14,560
We should run away.

131
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:16,450
Run away?

132
00:08:16,533 --> 00:08:17,500
From what?

133
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,240
From this town.

134
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:20,740
From the monsters.

135
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:23,120
From the moonlit black cats.

136
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:26,220
And from Sword Art Online, too.

137
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:29,180
Are you talking about suicide?

138
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:33,220
That's not such a bad idea.

139
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:37,417
Sorry, no.

140
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:42,206
If I had the guts to die, I wouldn't be
hiding in town where it's safe, would I?

141
00:08:43,660 --> 00:08:46,600
But really, why can't we just leave?

142
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:51,777
Why do we have to die when
it's just a stupid game?

143
00:08:51,860 --> 00:08:54,154
What's the point of going through this?

144
00:08:56,420 --> 00:08:59,020
Yeah, there is no point, I guess.

145
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:08,520
i i'm so afraid of dying in here
it's really that bad for you

146
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:14,440
i'm so scared i haven't been
able to get any sleep lately

147
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:21,957
you're not going to die
really how can you be so

148
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:25,160
sure about that the black
cats are strong enough

149
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:26,890
as a guild.

150
00:09:26,973 --> 00:09:29,717
Besides, our margin of safety
is well above the norm.

151
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:31,976
Plus, you got Tetsuo and me up front,

152
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:35,238
so there's no reason to be
on the frontlines with us.

153
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,917
You honestly don't think I'll die?

154
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,235
Will I make it back to the real world?

155
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:44,080
Yeah, you're not gonna die. You'll see.

156
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:46,754
We'll clear this game and go home soon.

157
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:02,470
Come in.

158
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:06,580
I'm sorry.

159
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:08,720
I can't seem to get to sleep.

160
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:13,040
If I stay in this guild,

161
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:17,299
she'll be safe, and we'll all make
it back to the real world someday.

162
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:22,040
There must be a lot of players like
her who are afraid of dying here.

163
00:10:22,880 --> 00:10:27,160
But still, they laugh and cry
and try to live as best they can.

164
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:30,591
I never thought about it like that before.

165
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:32,370
Kirito?

166
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:34,260
It's okay.

167
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:36,700
I promise you're going to survive.

168
00:10:42,660 --> 00:10:46,120
And no matter what, I promise
I'll protect all of you.

169
00:10:50,140 --> 00:10:51,500
Okay, I'm heading out.

170
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:53,050
Teleport!

171
00:10:53,133 --> 00:10:53,998
Town of Beginnings!

172
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:58,860
Can you believe it?

173
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:01,717
I never thought buying a
house would be so exciting!

174
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,682
Dude, you sound like an old man.

175
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:07,950
Hey,

176
00:11:08,033 --> 00:11:09,477
while Kato's off buying the house,

177
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:12,017
what do you guys say we go
out and raise some extra cash?

178
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:13,865
Oh, then we can buy furniture!

179
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:17,062
Come on, let's go to a
dungeon on a higher floor!

180
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:19,689
We should stick to our
usual hunting spots.

181
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:22,397
But up there, we could
make more and faster.

182
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:26,186
Yeah, and at our levels, we don't
have anything to worry about.

183
00:11:28,280 --> 00:11:29,110
You see?

184
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:31,477
I told you guys this was going to be cake.

185
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:34,437
We might even be able to
reach the front line sooner.

186
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:36,820
That's what I'm talking about. Look.

187
00:11:43,540 --> 00:11:44,380
No way.

188
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:45,620
A hidden door?

189
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:52,280
A treasure chest! Woo-hoo!

190
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:54,800
No, wait!

191
00:12:08,940 --> 00:12:10,440
It's a trap, guys!

192
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:11,930
Hurry!

193
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:13,317
Let's get out of here!

194
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:14,400
Teleport theft!

195
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:16,800
Teleport theft!

196
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:18,237
We can't use our crystals!

197
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:21,060
They're probably being
blocked by the walls

198
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:49,150
Yeah!

199
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:57,620
Stacia!

200
00:12:58,940 --> 00:13:00,340
Kiriko!

201
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,430
Stacia!

202
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:36,169
I hear someone's been taking
risks with their level raising.

203
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:38,680
You got any new info for me or what?

204
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:41,516
Nothing worth charging you money for.

205
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:44,120
You give info brokers a bad name.

206
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:46,317
Hey, this wasn't in the beta test.

207
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:47,377
It's a first-time event.

208
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:50,166
How am I supposed to
know what's gonna happen?

209
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:55,057
All I know is that tonight on Christmas
Eve, the event boss is gonna appear.

210
00:13:55,140 --> 00:13:56,937
He's called Nicholas the Renegade,

211
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:59,961
and he's gonna show up
under a fir tree somewhere.

212
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:04,221
The major guilds are searching
everywhere for the tree as we speak.

213
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:08,897
You wouldn't happen to know
where it is, would you?

214
00:14:08,980 --> 00:14:09,810
Maybe.

215
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:12,589
Are you thinking of
going solo on this one?

216
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:21,220
In this world, the dead
can never return to life.

217
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:24,880
I heard a rumor, though.

218
00:14:25,660 --> 00:14:30,601
If you beat Nicholas the Renegade, he'll
drop an item that can revive a dead player.

219
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:36,240
I'm going alone, and
I'll probably die alone.

220
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:39,616
No one will see me, no one will know.

221
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:41,727
Nothing will be left behind.

222
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:43,220
That's how I'll die.

223
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:44,680
You're a beater.

224
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:47,180
You had no right to be with us.

225
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:00,320
That's right.

226
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:02,120
It's my fault.

227
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:04,520
My arrogance killed you.

228
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:05,960
All of you.

229
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:12,020
If only I hadn't kept my true level
as a player secret from everyone.

230
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:18,228
I have to figure out a
way to beat Nicholas.

231
00:15:18,620 --> 00:15:20,560
Then I can revive Sachi.

232
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:24,400
And then I'll find out what
she was trying to tell me.

233
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:31,780
And if it turns out she
was cursing me, fine.

234
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:33,160
I accept it.

235
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:46,170
What's up?

236
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:48,400
You followed me? Of course.

237
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:51,371
You're after the revival item, aren't you?

238
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:52,490
Yeah.

239
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:57,153
Don't be risking your life for some
rumor that could turn out to be bogus.

240
00:15:57,900 --> 00:16:00,959
Man, you can't be messing
around in this death game.

241
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:03,220
Once your HP hits zero, that's it.

242
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:05,737
In the real world, your
brain gets fried and it's...

243
00:16:05,820 --> 00:16:06,650
Shut up.

244
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,037
I'm trying to get you to stop
with all your stupid soloing.

245
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:11,591
Come on, join up with us.

246
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:14,397
Whoever gets it to drop
the revival item keeps it.

247
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:15,480
No hard feelings.

248
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:17,168
Hey, that's fair, isn't it?

249
00:16:17,660 --> 00:16:19,640
But then, there'd be no point.

250
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:22,660
I have to do this. Alone.

251
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:26,637
Think about what you're doing, Kirito.

252
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:29,217
It's suicide, and I can't
let you die like that.

253
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:30,130
Come on!

254
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:38,500
I guess you were being followed,
too, huh, Klein? Uh-huh.

255
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:39,857
It sure looks that way.

256
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:41,920
It's the Holy Dragon Alliance.

257
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:45,537
They'll do anything for a rare
item, no matter how shady.

258
00:16:45,620 --> 00:16:46,460
What do we do?

259
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:48,520
You bastards.

260
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:52,560
Screw these guys!

261
00:16:52,860 --> 00:16:55,040
Get out of here, Kirito! No way.

262
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:56,497
Leave them to us.

263
00:16:56,580 --> 00:16:57,757
We can hold them off.

264
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:58,670
Get going!

265
00:17:18,840 --> 00:17:20,780
I don't know.

266
00:17:39,940 --> 00:17:40,770
Let's do this.

267
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,000
Kirito, hey!

268
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:17,817
There, that's the revival item.

269
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:22,760
Let's see; it says: "must
administer to affected player

270
00:18:23,620 --> 00:18:29,380
within 10 seconds." If someone dies in
front of you someday, make sure you use it!

271
00:18:44,260 --> 00:18:45,697
Kirito! Listen.

272
00:18:45,780 --> 00:18:47,400
Stay alive, you hear?

273
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:48,817
I don't care how you do it.

274
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:51,320
Just stay alive to the end.

275
00:18:57,520 --> 00:18:58,520
See ya.

276
00:19:20,420 --> 00:19:21,250
Saatchi…

277
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:34,480
Merry Christmas, Kirito.

278
00:19:36,540 --> 00:19:40,120
By the time you hear this,
I'll probably be dead.

279
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:43,540
How can I explain this?

280
00:19:44,020 --> 00:19:45,220
Let's see...

281
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:50,289
To tell you the truth, I never really
wanted to leave the town of beginnings.

282
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:55,186
And I knew if I fought with an attitude
like that, I would end up dying someday.

283
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:57,865
But that's not anyone's fault.

284
00:19:58,240 --> 00:20:00,416
That's something I have to deal with.

285
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:04,040
Kirito, ever since that
night you found me,

286
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:07,693
you kept telling me I wasn't
going to die no matter what.

287
00:20:08,820 --> 00:20:10,437
But what if I got killed anyway?

288
00:20:10,520 --> 00:20:13,108
I knew that if I died,
you'd blame yourself.

289
00:20:13,260 --> 00:20:16,140
That's why I decided
to record this for you.

290
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:21,997
By the way, I know how
powerful you really are. Sorry.

291
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:24,551
I sort of peaked when you weren't looking.

292
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:27,717
I wondered why you
weren't telling the truth

293
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:29,957
about what level player you really were.

294
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:32,628
I wondered why you
decided to fight with us.

295
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:34,544
I never figured it out, though.

296
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:36,700
You know what?

297
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:40,917
When I found out how strong you were,
I don't know, it made me so happy.

298
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,220
I felt relieved.

299
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:47,720
So even if I die, promise me
you'll go on living, okay, Kirito?

300
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:53,317
Stay alive, so you can see the end of this
world and find out why it was created.

301
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:56,106
Find out why a weakling
like me ended up here.

302
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:58,660
Find out the reason you and I met.

303
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:00,450
Please.

304
00:21:01,500 --> 00:21:02,680
That's what I wish.

305
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:08,673
Looks like I still have time, so seeing
how it's Christmas and everything,

306
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:10,195
I'll sing you a song.

307
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:47,837
Anyway, Kirito, I'm so glad I met you.

308
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:51,740
And that I could be with
you, even for a little while.

309
00:21:53,220 --> 00:21:55,600
Thank you, goodbye.

310
00:22:15,660 --> 00:22:18,460
Let's go.

311
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:38,200
Next time, the Black Swordsman
